            "tags": [],
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 19282,
            "text": "When `from` and `to` are specified, `seq.int()` returns a compact ALTREP vector, but the same isn't true when `from` and `length.out` are specified, making the latter massively slower.\n\nThis caught me by surprise and I suspect most R users also won't expect this. The \"fix\" is to use the less readable alternative, where `to` is manually computed to be passed to `seq.int()`.\n\nAs far as I can tell, it should be possible & sensible to return a compact ALTREP vector in both cases, as long as only these two arguments are specified.\n\n``` r\nstart <- 2026L\n\nbench::mark(\n  seq.int(start, 1e7+start-1L),\n  seq.int(start, length.out = 1e7)\n)\n#> # A tibble: 2 × 6\n#>   expression                            min  median `itr/sec` mem_alloc `gc/sec`\n#>   <bch:expr>                        <bch:t> <bch:t>     <dbl> <bch:byt>    <dbl>\n#> 1 seq.int(start, 1e+07 + start - 1…   121ns   158ns 4936346.         0B      0  \n#> 2 seq.int(start, length.out = 1e+0…  15.5ms  16.3ms      60.4    38.1MB     60.4\n\n.Internal(inspect(seq.int(start, 1e7+start-1L)))\n#> @6227e5b42718 13 INTSXP g0c0 [REF(65535)]  2026 : 10002025 (compact)\n.Internal(inspect(seq.int(start, length.out = 1e7)))\n#> @71ff0a226010 13 INTSXP g0c7 [] (len=10000000, tl=0) 2026,2027,2028,2029,2030,...\n```",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-04T15:15:02Z",
            "creator": "hugo.gruson+Rbugzilla"
          },
          {
            "text": "I messed up formatting of the code block in my previous message. Apologies.\n\n```\nstart <- 2026L\n\nbench::mark(\n  seq.int(start, 1e7+start-1L),\n  seq.int(start, length.out = 1e7)\n)\n#> # A tibble: 2 × 6\n#>   expression                            min  median `itr/sec` mem_alloc `gc/sec`\n#>   <bch:expr>                        <bch:t> <bch:t>     <dbl> <bch:byt>    <dbl>\n#> 1 seq.int(start, 1e+07 + start - 1…   121ns   158ns 4936346.         0B      0  \n#> 2 seq.int(start, length.out = 1e+0…  15.5ms  16.3ms      60.4    38.1MB     60.4\n\n.Internal(inspect(seq.int(start, 1e7+start-1L)))\n#> @6227e5b42718 13 INTSXP g0c0 [REF(65535)]  2026 : 10002025 (compact)\n.Internal(inspect(seq.int(start, length.out = 1e7)))\n#> @71ff0a226010 13 INTSXP g0c7 [] (len=10000000, tl=0) 2026,2027,2028,2029,2030,...\n```",
            "bug_id": 19282,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 1,
            "creator": "hugo.gruson+Rbugzilla",
