          {
            "creation_time": "2026-11-10T01:17:16Z",
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "count": 2,
            "is_markdown": false,
            "bug_id": 19282,
            "text": "Created attachment 4023\npatch: return compact sequences from seq.int() with length.out\n\nAgreed, and this is cheap to do: by the time do_seq() handles length.out it has already computed the endpoints and decided the result is the integer sequence from:to, but then allocates and fills the whole vector instead of calling seq_colon() as seq.int(from, to) does.\n\nThe attached patch (against r90865) routes the length.out cases whose result is exactly from:to -- by missing, or by = +/- 1 -- through seq_colon(), so seq.int(from, length.out = n) and the to= / unit-step from,to variants now return compact sequences. Values and types are unchanged, and endpoints that do not round-trip keep the old code. Includes a regression test; make check passes.\n\nPatch also at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/464",
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": 4023,
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 104141,
            "time": "2026-11-10T01:17:16Z"
